  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how much Judy will spend on pencils over 45 days, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the number of pencils Judy uses per day:**\n   Judy uses 10 pencils in 5 days. Therefore, the number of pencils she uses per day is:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{10 \\text{ pencils}}{5 \\text{ days}} = 2 \\text{ pencils/day}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the total number of pencils Judy will use over 45 days:**\n   Since Judy uses 2 pencils per day, over 45 days she will use:\n   \\[\n   2 \\text{ pencils/day} \\times 45 \\text{ days} = 90 \\text{ pencils}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Determine how many 30-pack sets of pencils Judy needs:**\n   A 30-pack of pencils costs $4. To find out how many 30-pack sets Judy needs to buy to get at least 90 pencils, we divide the total number of pencils by the number of pencils in a pack:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{90 \\text{ pencils}}{30 \\text{ pencils/pack}} = 3 \\text{ packs}\n   \\]\n   Since 3 packs are needed, the total cost will be:\n   \\[\n   3 \\text{ packs} \\times 4 \\text{ dollars/pack} = 12 \\text{ dollars}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the total amount Judy will spend on pencils over 45 days is \\(\\boxed{12}\\).",
